{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games","id":966472,"title":"How much is known about Black Dog Game Factory's World of Shadow games?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T16:16:34-07:00","id":966472,"title":"How much is known about Black Dog Game Factory's World of Shadow games?","content":"I've been reading up on Black Dog Game Factory in a number of Werewolf supplements (Book of the Wyrm, A Guide to Pentex) and <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Black_Dog_Game_Factory_(Pentex)\" target=\"_blank\">the Wikia</a>, so I know the names of the various games. But what is known about their premises, or how the games roughly work? Are there maybe other books with more information about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:01:22-07:00","id":966489,"title":"","content":"For the most part I think Black Dog was put in the game as a kind of meta joke (as were the fomori their game books create). I'm sure it's roughly as popular (or, in a sense, unpopular) as the World of Darkness series is in our reality. Of course you can adjust as needed... I can see arguments for it being even smaller and more niche inside the WoD since many elements of society are more of a caricature of themselves in-game (and because White Wolf really enjoyed poking fun at themselves... just look at the authors' self-deprecating parodies)... or you might rule that Black Dog sort of covers and represents all RPGs inside the WoD, in which case it might be a bit more prevalent.<br /> <br /> Either way, do try to avoid characters running down to their local game shop to get the latest Revenant core book to learn all Kindred's secrets and weaknesses...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:18:07-07:00","id":966494,"title":"","content":"Well in reality, Black Dog had become a sub set of White Wolf. They actually published books under the label Black Dog. Freak Legion: A Players Guide to Fomori, and few Dark Ages supplements, and Dark Kingdom of Rust: Austiwtch ( I so know I spelled that Nazi Camp's wrong...) for Wraith. <br /> As far as in game, Black Dog was left...open. So that the ST could develop it as they saw fit. I believe mostly done that way because, as Crusher mentioned, it was a inside joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T17:59:42-07:00","id":966504,"title":"","content":"It's primarily in Subsidiaries. Over the course of the line, some writers have also given different names for the same &quot;slot&quot; of WoD game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:58:52-07:00","id":966682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966489#post966489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, do try to avoid characters running down to their local game shop to get the latest Revenant core book to learn all Kindred's secrets and weaknesses...</div> </div> </div> </div>From one of the sources I read there are occational truths in the books they write, like the location of a Haven or an actual summoning ritual. But they are few and far between and not added intentionally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966494#post966494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in reality, Black Dog had become a sub set of White Wolf. They actually published books under the label Black Dog. Freak Legion: A Players Guide to Fomori, and few Dark Ages supplements, and Dark Kingdom of Rust: Austiwtch ( I so know I spelled that Nazi Camp's wrong...) for Wraith. As far as in game, Black Dog was left...open. So that the ST could develop it as they saw fit. I believe mostly done that way because, as Crusher mentioned, it was a inside joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am aware of the real-life Black Dog and the more... risque books they release.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966504#post966504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's primarily in Subsidiaries. Over the course of the line, some writers have also given different names for the same &quot;slot&quot; of WoD game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Wikia names all the games known, which match pretty much all games with X: The Y titles.<br /> <br /> Except Mummy, because even in-universe nobody seems to care about Mummy: The Resurrection.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T04:58:01-07:00","id":966710,"title":"","content":"Well, Mummies were rare before the Revised era. I mean, there is only so much you can do with a splat with 50+ members. That is by definition a group of special little snowflakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T06:13:11-07:00","id":966725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966710#post966710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Mummies were rare before the Revised era. I mean, there is only so much you can do with a splat with 50+ members. That is by definition a group of special little snowflakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>But if that's the case, how can Demon have a Black Dog counterpart while Mummy doesn't?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T09:56:01-07:00","id":966801,"title":"","content":"Because Demon fits into the sick and twisted narratives of Black Dog more than Mummy? In the Demon counterpart, I imagine you are a Demon who is spreading evil throughout the world by rewarding mass murderers and serial rapists with demonic pacts that grants them otherworldly powers in exchange for the mystical energy, Corruption, generated by their evil deeds. It probably would also reward you for engaging in mass murder and serial rape by allowing you to recover Corruption more quickly by personally committing violations against human beings (with violations against children and infants granting you even greater amounts of Corruption).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T10:45:36-07:00","id":966827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games#post966472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been reading up on Black Dog Game Factory in a number of Werewolf supplements (Book of the Wyrm, A Guide to Pentex) and <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Black_Dog_Game_Factory_(Pentex)\" target=\"_blank\">the Wikia</a>, so I know the names of the various games. But what is known about their premises, or how the games roughly work? Are there maybe other books with more information about them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is about all you need to know when it comes to figuring out how they work. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.warosu.org/data/tg/img/0369/93/1419655968784.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:47:09-07:00","id":966904,"title":"","content":"I would only ever use the in-setting Black Dog Game Factory if I needed a plot where RPGs were really getting players involved with the &quot;real world&quot; occult of the WoD. Otherwise, why bother?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:59:32-07:00","id":966968,"title":"","content":"Hm, a potential plot hook. Adolescent Kinfolk are starting to get into a new RPG, Succubi: the Submission, which actively encourages a very involved form of LARP. The characters are drawn into the subculture of Succubi: the Submission, which celebrates sexual exploration and sexual liberation.<br /> <br /> The goal of Black Dog Games is to produce a reactionary backlash by concerned parents (to encourage alienation and rebellious behavior among adolescents). They offer free PDF versions of Succubi: The Submission with the PG-13 rated artwork (the R rated artwork can only be found in the softcover print vetsions while the NC-17 rated artwork can only be found in the hardcover versions). Within the PDF versions of the corebook are sufficient instructions for sorcerers to develop the Mythic Numina of Fascination 1-2, the softcover versions Fascination 1-4, and the hardcover versions Fascination 1-6. Each additional publication contains instructions for a different Mythic Numina, with the greater secrets being found in the more explicit versions of the same book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:14:53-07:00","id":966976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966968#post966968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, a potential plot hook. Adolescent Kinfolk are starting to get into a new RPG, Succubi: the Submission, which actively encourages a very involved form of LARP. The characters are drawn into the subculture of Succubi: the Submission, which celebrates sexual exploration and sexual liberation.<br /> <br /> The goal of Black Dog Games is to produce a reactionary backlash by concerned parents (to encourage alienation and rebellious behavior among adolescents). They offer free PDF versions of Succubi: The Submission with the PG-13 rated artwork (the R rated artwork can only be found in the softcover print vetsions while the NC-17 rated artwork can only be found in the hardcover versions). Within the PDF versions of the corebook are sufficient instructions for sorcerers to develop the Mythic Numina of Fascination 1-2, the softcover versions Fascination 1-4, and the hardcover versions Fascination 1-6. Each additional publication contains instructions for a different Mythic Numina, with the greater secrets being found in the more explicit versions of the same book.</div> </div> </div> </div>RE: Mystic Numina, are you talking about things that characters in the game within the game are using, or things that characters played by the players will be picking up? Because if it's the latter, it shouldn't be more than a dot or two of Occult, and maybe one dot on a path.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T16:25:41-07:00","id":966980,"title":"","content":"Well, the idea would be that the illustrations found within the books would give insight into highly sexual magical practices that would allow players of the game to develop the Mythic Numina with repeated practice. In effect, Black Dog Games would be trying to give the secrets of linear magic to horny adolescents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:39:17-07:00","id":967014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966980#post966980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the idea would be that the illustrations found within the books would give insight into highly sexual magical practices that would allow players of the game to develop the Mythic Numina with repeated practice. In effect, Black Dog Games would be trying to give the secrets of linear magic to horny adolescents.</div> </div> </div> </div>That said, I can't see anyone on their in-world payroll being particularly effective at it, since they were described as not actually believing in the subject of their writing. Even the secret cannibal (and BSD kinfolk) Evan Stump probably doesn't know where those old recipies for long pig really came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T17:51:26-07:00","id":967019,"title":"","content":"Well, the idea is how would an effective and threatening Black Dog Games look, not what the current inside joke would do. Though I could see the case being made for an Infernalist infiltrating their company for the purpose of spreading true occult knowledge, as the slow progression will drive impatient gamers to her mistress (a Demon Queen specifically named in the books).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T18:10:41-07:00","id":967034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=967019#post967019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the idea is how would an effective and threatening Black Dog Games look, not what the current inside joke would do. Though I could see the case being made for an Infernalist infiltrating their company for the purpose of spreading true occult knowledge, as the slow progression will drive impatient gamers to her mistress (a Demon Queen specifically named in the books).</div> </div> </div> </div>Even an effective and threatening BDGF isn't nearly as effective or threatening as other subsidiaries. Perhaps not to the extent of being a complete joke, but there's something to the Beavis-style Carnage entry in Subsidiaries pointing out that no one at the company (except for the Iliad fomor kung fu master president) being a significant combatant or influential monstrous creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:09:18-07:00","id":967111,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, a major part of what makes Pentex and the Wyrm so terrifying and certain-to-victory ISN'T their overt plots, fomori factories, and Captain Planet-villain antics. If anything, the handful of times a loyal O'Tolley's customer finds themselves barfing face-eating hook worms in the toilet isn't the the grande scheme coming to a head, but an accidental side effect and outlier to the big picture... and an inconvenience to the Corporation that has to be addressed. Because the best way to spread as much taint as possible isn't for King's Liquor customers to start grabbing lead pipes and going on roid-rage murder sprees... That draws attention, and eventually someone somewhere might start making connections. But if King's Liquor is the 2nd largest beer seller in the US, reaching the refrigerators of 160 million Americans, and their customers are 15% more likely to be instigators of domestic violence or rape... well... not only is that a LOT more net suffering in the world as a whole, but let's not forget the gradual and creeping side effects that abuse can cause later down-the-line.*<br /> <br /> No, Pentex has been dominating the slow game on a level the Garou probably can barely begin to fathom... to the degree that up until the newer themes of &quot;hope&quot; were even introduced, it's hard for anyone with all the details to see a scenario in which they don't win. They're already a hundred moves ahead.<br /> <br /> That's not to say Pentex can't or doesn't make those types of obvious moves.... it's a massive bureaucracy with thousands of management-types who each have their own ideas as how to best serve the wyrm (with the remaining tens- or hundreds-of-thousands of direct or indirect employees left oblivious)... but point is, not everything has to be a direct and blatant path to corruption. Maybe Black Dog's biggest service is fostering teen angst, identity crises, and violent ideations.<br /> <br /> *Edit: In case there's question, these figures are made up for the sake of illustration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12162,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","user":"Crusher-of-Cities","date":". 09-10-2016, 11:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:40:07-07:00","id":967528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/966472-how-much-is-known-about-black-dog-game-factory-s-world-of-shadow-games?p=966968#post966968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, a potential plot hook. Adolescent Kinfolk are starting to get into a new RPG, Succubi: the Submission, which actively encourages a very involved form of LARP. The characters are drawn into the subculture of Succubi: the Submission, which celebrates sexual exploration and sexual liberation.<br /> <br /> The goal of Black Dog Games is to produce a reactionary backlash by concerned parents (to encourage alienation and rebellious behavior among adolescents). They offer free PDF versions of Succubi: The Submission with the PG-13 rated artwork (the R rated artwork can only be found in the softcover print vetsions while the NC-17 rated artwork can only be found in the hardcover versions). Within the PDF versions of the corebook are sufficient instructions for sorcerers to develop the Mythic Numina of Fascination 1-2, the softcover versions Fascination 1-4, and the hardcover versions Fascination 1-6. Each additional publication contains instructions for a different Mythic Numina, with the greater secrets being found in the more explicit versions of the same book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiousity, what book is the Fascination Numina from?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:00:30-07:00","id":967581,"title":"","content":"There is one version in Sorcerer: The Hedge Magician's Handbook and a different version in Sorcerer (Revised).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}